        <adventure.version>5.2.0</adventure.version>
        <!-- Do not bump without reading the CI log's "Tests run:" line, not just its
             green tick. 3.6.0 once discovered ZERO tests on the Linux runner: surefire
             printed "Tests run: 0" and exited 0, so the build looked green and six PRs
             merged that way (issue #39), including the ones fixing 50 test failures.

             What the logs actually showed, compared run-for-run on the same commit:
               3.5.3  provider selected, then 26 "Running <class>" lines, 188 tests
               3.6.0  provider selected, then no "Running" line at all, 0 tests
             The same 33 test sources compiled in both, and the same
             JUnitPlatformProvider was auto-detected in both — so this was test
             *selection*, not a fork that failed to start and not a missing engine.

             Two things had to change for 3.6.0 to be safe here, and both are load-
             bearing:
               1. The custom <includes> block was removed (see the plugin config
                  below). Its single "**/*Test.java" pattern made surefire translate a
                  source-shaped pattern into the .class names it scans — the one
                  discovery step that changed behaviour between these versions. The
                  defaults already match this suite, so nothing is lost.
               2. build.yml no longer passes -DfailIfNoTests=false, and an "Enforce test
                  outcome" step now actually fails the job on an empty suite. The old
                  guard computed test_exit_code=1 for exactly this case but no step
                  consumed it, so it was correct and inert.

             A local run is not proof either way: 3.6.0 runs all 188 tests on Windows
             with an identical command, and has always done so. Only the runner's log
             can confirm a version bump. That asymmetry is why the guard in (2) matters
             more than any pin — it makes the failure loud instead of silent.

             Dependabot's maven-minor-patch group still excludes this artifact, but the
             exclusion is now belt-and-braces rather than the only defence. -->
        <surefire.version>3.6.0</surefire.version>
    </properties>

